## Dev-only: let SECUREDROP_DEV_VM drive @tag:sd-workstation qubes (scripts/try-pr.py).
## Installed by `make dev-vm-policy`. Never use on a production workstation.
#
# Numbered 30 so it's evaluated before the SecureDrop Workstation policies
# (31-*, 32-*), whose catch-all deny rules would otherwise match first.

qubes.VMShell      *  SECUREDROP_DEV_VM  @tag:sd-workstation  allow
# vm.run() checks the qube's OS to know how to end the shell command
admin.vm.feature.CheckWithTemplate  +os  SECUREDROP_DEV_VM  @tag:sd-workstation  allow target=dom0

admin.vm.List      *  SECUREDROP_DEV_VM  @adminvm             allow target=dom0
admin.vm.List      *  SECUREDROP_DEV_VM  @tag:sd-workstation  allow target=dom0
admin.vm.CurrentState  *  SECUREDROP_DEV_VM  @tag:sd-workstation  allow target=dom0
admin.vm.tag.Get   *  SECUREDROP_DEV_VM  @tag:sd-workstation  allow target=dom0
admin.vm.property.Get  +is_preload  SECUREDROP_DEV_VM  @tag:sd-workstation  allow target=dom0
admin.vm.Shutdown  *  SECUREDROP_DEV_VM  @tag:sd-workstation  allow target=dom0
admin.vm.Start     *  SECUREDROP_DEV_VM  @tag:sd-workstation  allow target=dom0
